Smart Pantry Manager - Husna Mohamed, 402310405
An Android app written in Java that helps reduce food waste.
The user records the ingredients they already have at home (their "pantry"),
and the app suggests only the recipes they can cook right now using those ingredients.
No shopping trip needed.

Features
    Pantry management: add, edit and delete ingredients (name, quantity, unit and an optional expiry date)
    Pantry list: a RecyclerView with a custom adapter, loaded from the database
    20 pre-loaded recipes: seeded into the database the first time the app runs
    Strict matching: a recipe is suggested only if every ingredient is in the pantry in at least the required quantity. If a recipe needs 5 ingredients and the pantry has 4, it is not shown
    Robust matching: handles singular/plural names (tomato / tomatoes) and unit differences (kg / g, tbsp / tsp, ml / l)
    Recipe detail screen: full ingredient list and method
    Empty-state messages: a clear message when the pantry is empty or when no recipes match
    Settings screen: toggle for expiring-soon alerts
    Input validation: on the add/edit form (blank name, letters only, quantity must be a number above 0)
    Bottom navigation bar: Pantry, Recipes and Settings

Database choice: SQLite
I chose SQLite (using SQLiteOpenHelper) because:
    1.it runs locally on the device, so there is no server to build, host or pay for
    2.it works fully offline, which suits a pantry app used in the kitchen
    3.data is stored in a file on the phone, so it persists after the app is closed and reopened
    4.it is the approach covered in the module's persistent data chapter

Tables
    Table	            Columns
    pantry	            id, name, quantity, unit, expiry
    recipes	            id, name, steps
    recipe_ingredients	id, recipe_id (FK to recipes), name, quantity, unit

How the strict-matching rule works
RecipeMatcher.canMake() loops through every ingredient a recipe needs. For each one it:
    1.normalises the name (lower case, trimmed, plural turned into singular)
    2.adds up the matching pantry entries, converting units to a common base (g, ml or pcs)
    3.returns false immediately if the amount in the pantry is less than the amount needed
A recipe is suggested only if the loop finishes without returning false.

Project structure
    app/src/main/java/com/example/smartpantrymanager/
        PantryItem.java, Recipe.java, RecipeIngredient.java   (models)
        DatabaseHelper.java                                   (SQLite, CRUD, seed data)
        RecipeMatcher.java                                    (strict-matching logic)
        PantryAdapter.java, RecipeAdapter.java                (RecyclerView adapters)
        BaseActivity.java                                     (shared bottom navigation)
        MainActivity.java                                     (pantry list)
        AddEditItemActivity.java                              (add / edit form)
        SuggestedRecipesActivity.java                         (strict suggestions)
        RecipeDetailActivity.java                             (recipe detail)
        SettingsActivity.java                                 (settings)
    app/src/main/res/layout/                                  (screen and row layouts)
    app/src/main/res/menu/bottom_nav_menu.xml                 (navigation menu)
    Setup and run instructions

Requirements: Android Studio (recent version), JDK bundled with Android Studio, and an emulator or physical device running Android 7.0 (API 24) or higher.
    1. Clone this repository:
        git clone https://github.com/[husii-04]/SmartPantryManager.git
    2.Open Android Studio and choose Open, then select the cloned SmartPantryManager folder.
    3.Wait for the Gradle sync to finish.
    4.Create an emulator in Device Manager (Pixel 6, API 24 or higher), or connect a physical device with USB debugging turned on.
    5.Wait until the emulator has fully started and shows the home screen.
    6.Press the green Run button.
    No API keys, accounts or internet connection are needed.

Testing the strict matching
    Add Egg 2 pcs, Bread 2 pcs, Butter 10 g and Salt 1 tsp.
    Open Recipes: Scrambled Eggs on Toast appears.
    Delete Salt and open Recipes again: the recipe disappears.
    Add Salt back and the recipe returns.
    Close and reopen the app: the pantry data is still there.

Tech
    Java, Android Studio
    SQLite via SQLiteOpenHelper
    RecyclerView with custom adapters
    Material Components (BottomNavigationView, MaterialCardView)
    SharedPreferences for the settings toggle